  "prediction": "The report examines the use of Electronic Advance Data (EAD) by the United States Postal Service (USPS) and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) to target mail for inspection. The report found that while USPS and CBP have been using EAD in pilots since 2016, there are no clear performance goals or data on the pilots' effectiveness. The report also noted that the costs of collecting and using EAD are unclear, and USPS and CBP have not assessed the benefits of using EAD compared to other methods of mail selection for inspection. The report recommends that USPS and CBP establish performance goals for the pilots, collect data on their effectiveness, and assess the costs and benefits of using EAD compared to other methods of mail selection for inspection. The Department of Homeland Security concurred with the recommendations. The report also mentions that USPS has faced financial challenges in recent years, adding to the importance of carefully considering the costs and benefits of using EAD for mail selection for inspection.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report examines the use of Electronic Advance Data (EAD) by the United States Postal Service (USPS) and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) to target mail for inspection. The report found that while USPS and CBP have been using EAD in pilots since 2016, there are no clear performance goals or data on the pilots' effectiveness. The report also noted that the costs of collecting and using EAD are unclear, and USPS and CBP have not assessed the benefits of using EAD compared to other methods of mail selection for inspection. The report recommends that USPS and CBP establish performance goals for the pilots, collect data on their effectiveness, and assess the costs and benefits of using EAD compared to other methods of mail selection for inspection. The Department of Homeland Security concurred with the recommendations. The report also mentions that USPS has faced financial challenges in recent years, adding to the importance of carefully considering the costs and benefits of using EAD for mail selection for inspection.",
